.TH QUANUXCTL-SPREADER-DEPLOY 1 "February 2026" "QuanuX 1.0.0" "QuanuX Commands"
.SH NAME
quanuxctl-spreader-deploy \- Authenticate and transmit a Spreader binary to a live Execution Node.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B quanuxctl spreader deploy
.I <BINARY_NAME>
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B quanuxctl spreader deploy
authenticates a pre-compiled High-Frequency Spreader binary against its cryptographic forge signature and transmits it over the ZeroMQ / NATS topology to a bare-metal execution node.

Because the Cython Forge translates user JSON into hardware-specific C++ machine code, dynamic loading is impossible. The engine must be holistically compiled and securely delivered.
.SH CRYPTOGRAPHIC VALIDATION (SHM GATE)
When a user or agent invokes `deploy`, the command executes an isolated SHA-256 validation scan.

1.  Locates the requested `<BINARY_NAME>` inside the CMake build tree.
2.  Locates the corresponding `<BINARY_NAME>.sig` manifest originally generated by `quanuxctl spreader package`.
3.  Calculates the runtime hash of the binary file and cross-references it against the signature string.

If the validation succeeds, the binary is routed to the Execution Node.
If the validation fails, deployment is aborted with `CRITICAL SHM ERROR: Binary checksum mismatch. Forgery detected!`. This unconditionally prevents bloated or altered executables from destroying the 59ns latency profile.
